  "name": "Zig",
  "description": "A general-purpose programming language and toolchain designed for robustness, optimality, and reusability through a unique compile-time metaprogramming system and explicit resource management. It functions as a drop-in C/C++ compiler with built-in cross-compilation support, featuring a self-hosting compiler architecture and a zero-dependency standard library. The codebase includes extensive runtime support for diverse hardware architectures and low-level system integrations.",
